8","84d3bff3980990d7","84df3eaa0c722cc6","84e1cc4ff49df89d","84e1cc4ff49df89d","84e1cc4ff49df89d","84e1cc4ff49df89d","84e1cc4ff49df89d","84e1cc4ff49df89d","84e1cc4ff49df89d","85367e5fd9147732","871b4fb0020336aa","8d9453495f3b0a72","8f512eba47111909","910db0c97d3a80af","918b78b95ee4148e","9665c6e172f6d5a1","9665c6e172f6d5a1","96993cdb927817c3","96993cdb927817c3","9718145f6cbb9c32","979cb686b847d02f","97e2bbc4e6d80ed9","995023c59bbcabf1","9bc253a9f7b4a76d","9de52a154da8c07b","9de52a154da8c07b","9ffeddfd04a27e74","a83eda53547dc4b2","ab5e997ca06ef1b9","ac07a7eda7dfb075","b04e50a2be22b48d","b1295def3e295abb","b167a5407ce70e07","b1c4f81b0d16c0ab","b2e3ffa978fb0a05","b6254536e2e914cd","ba2e18a93b55e425","bbbfc0abc947c221","bbc26e4be189809c","bd5d72362f2f4d1c","bdecc77a30cacf2b","be68d4d5802685c6","be9206ff2ec903fe","bebee3a31ab24d02","bf19a0807470ee59","c1bdc94df9039885","c6b3dc30f427846e","c7a989f4a17beb2c","c880b52139b1f90d","d0b8adfa320b08a6","d27ceba84657c916","d27ceba84657c916","d27ceba84657c916","d27ceba84657c916","d5652ba94a4b8729","d6317bf4a504eb97","d8b6a30ee337770c","deb56a3c0ccf2799","df07d2be697a39eb","df76f8dc38dada1a","e401b31a19806a3f","e5950bacb1415933","e65e6141de9a2917","e6c44f05060d9c2e","e8096bb083ea2f95","e8470868e4864f32","ed442cbbf83fb9e8","f069288f9a1abcf7","f12cb4754835f1e8","f2056e747d3dcd7e","f490417db9178e29","f5557bb18d6c579e","f864f93c1dc7ff05","f872f87024321261","faea5bec476bc90a","fb46da0659e9508a","ff8224f6ace70c68","ffc9a8405957e808"],"groups":["ba13abbc9a808a23","d673909f7cfe8d18","e25382fdf1bcf8cb","7acbf51a16bd3b6a","d470f659b73b1f64","60aba18dac754dcc","a4e4836471131ee2","bef196ee08aaced5"],"findings":"**Review of the git timeout and test group-kill change**\n\nI ran no new test suite. The orchestrator's full run (323/323) stands. I only ran two quick checks, both on this machine (GNU coreutils 9.11, Node).\n\n**1. Mismatch: timeouts are swallowed by `GlossError` catches in carry (group `git-timeout`) — read**\n\nThe notes say a timeout \"prints cleanly\" because callers run under the `GlossError` handler. That is true for the CLI, but not for code that catches `GlossError` to mean \"this gloss is unreadable\":\n- `src/commands/carry.ts:23-24`, `targetState()`: `if (err instanceof GlossError) return 'broken'`. A timed-out `readNote` (which rethrows the timeout via `rawNote` → `git()`) is reported as a broken gloss on the target.\n- `src/commands/carry.ts:42-44`, `carry()`: the same catch pushes the source into `unreadable`, so a hung `git notes show` becomes \"skipped sources whose gloss can't be read: <sha> (git notes --ref … timed out after …)\". The carry then goes ahead and writes from the remaining sources, without failing.\n\nSo a hung git during carry can silently drop a source and write a partial result, instead of failing with the timeout. The fix is the same pattern the change already uses in `sync.ts` and `gitTry`: rethrow when `err instanceof GitError && err.timedOut` in both catches. The notes don't list this caller. Its test would be a fake hanging `notes` in a carry test, which I did not run.\n\n**2. Claim check: wrapped sync children on a timeout — verified, no mismatch**\n\nThe `expired()` check depends on `timeout --signal=KILL` ending with SIGKILL. I checked it: `timeout --signal=KILL 1 sleep 5` exits 137, and `spawnSync` of the same command returns `signal: 'SIGKILL'`, `status: null`. So the \"timed out after N ms\" error fires as the notes say. This holds on this coreutils version; it is not verified on others.\n\n**3. Missing risk: Ctrl-C does not reach the wrapped group — read**\n\n`timeout` without `--foreground` runs its child in its own process group. A terminal Ctrl-C goes to the test runner's foreground group, so the wrapper and its git/CLI children may never see SIGINT. They would then run until the 120 s limit (plus the wrapper's own bound) after the runner exits. This is bounded, but it is not in the author's risk list. I did not reproduce it.\n\n**4. Checked, no issue — verified by grep**\n- No `shell: true` is used in `test/` or `src/`, so the `wrap()` arg-joining path is not exercised with a shell.\n- Async `spawn` calls in `test/ary.test.ts`, `test/untrusted.test.ts`, `test/reviews.test.ts` and `test/batch.test.ts` are not wrapped, as the notes say.\n\n**5. Read, minor:** the test's `gone()` helper and `alive()` use `/proc`, so these tests are Linux-only. This is not listed in the notes.\n\n**Necessity grading and removal candidates:** skipped per the review rules.\n\nNot verified: the carry behaviour in item 1 (I read the code paths only), and Ctrl-C behaviour in item 3.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
