nder `timeout`. A command that doesn't exist now gives `status 127` instead of the `ENOENT` error that `spawnSync` returned before, and `execFileSync` throws a different error. A test that checks for a missing binary through these helpers would see the changed behaviour.\n\n3. **Minor, read.** The new 120 s default limit applies to every git call, including slow operations on very large repos. It can fail a legitimate `git` call. The error does name `GIT_GLOSS_GIT_TIMEOUT`, so the user can raise the limit.\n\nVERDICT: CLEAN","verdict":"clean"}
